    "title": "Special Weather Statement by NWS - NewsBreak",
    "text": "Check NWS updates here At 947 PM CDT, Doppler radar was tracking strong thunderstorms along a line extending from 5 miles east of Winside to 4 miles south of West Point to 2 miles northeast of Colon. Movement was northeast at 30 mph. HAZARD...Wind gusts up to 50 mph and pea size hail. SOURCE...Radar indicated. IMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around unsecured objects. Minor hail damage to vegetation is possible. * Locations impacted include... Fremont, Blair, West Point, Tekamah, Bennington, Valley, Oakland, Arlington, North Bend, Wisner, Pender, Fort Calhoun, Scribner, Lyons, Emerson, Hooper, Walthill, Winnebago, Beemer, and Cedar Bluffs. This includes Interstate 29 between mile markers 66 and 72.",
